      "2. Epistemology of 'Attested Function': Force the panel to define 'attested function in French orthography'. A joke by Voltaire or aristocratic affectation on proper names does not make something an 'attested function of French orthography'. The circumflex was created and codified exclusively for phonological aperture, length, compensatory deletion, and disambiguation.",
